WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.260
- Hi everyone I'm Dan
Tieu, from Khan Academy.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.580
Unfortunately after
about a month and a half,

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.220
Sal's unable to join us today,

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.320
but you do have myself

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.240
and another Khan Academy
team member, Meaghan Pattani,

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.830
who's here to kinda hold down
the fort while Sal's away

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.400
and he'll be joining us tomorrow,
so don't worry about that.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.460
Before we get started if
you have any questions,

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.370
please start putting
them into the comment box

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.150
and the team will surface the
questions for us to answer

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.028
and we'll do our best to
do our Sal impersonations.

00:00:48.028 --> 00:00:49.380
(laughs)

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.280
So, for those of you who are
joining us for the first time,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.440
this is just a way for
us to stay connected,

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.160
especially at a time of social distancing

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.810
and school closers.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.050
Khan Academy's a non-profit,

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.350
with a mission to provide everyone a free,

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.850
world class education to anyone, anywhere.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.020
And the way we've been doing
that for the last 10 plus years

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.890
is really by creating
resources from Pre-K,

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:11.950
with Khan Academy Kids,

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.300
through Elementary school,
Middle school and High school.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.950
Covering courses in Math, ELA,
Humanities, Sciences and more

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.660
and when this crisis hit we recognized

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.850
that it was our duty to do even more.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.910
We've created daily
schedules and learning plans

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.370
to help provide structures
for remote learning.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:30.260
We've recorded parent and
teacher webinars in mass,

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.850
to provide guidance and
answer pressing questions

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.420
and we've even launched Khan
Academy Kids YouTube channel

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.270
with daily circle time, and
all of this in an effort

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:41.200
to keep everyone learning
through school closers.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.370
I wanna remind everyone
that we are non-profit,

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.210
we're funded by Philanthropic donations

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:48.670
by folks like yourself, and
we were running at a deficit

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:52.180
before the crisis and we've
seen our surfer usages increase

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.680
two to three times what we normally incur

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.860
and what that means is we
also have increased costs.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:59.490
And I wanna send a special shout-out

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.160
to several organizations who
were the some of the first

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.360
to step up and help us during this crisis.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:07.255
So Bank of America, Google.org,

00:02:07.255 --> 00:02:10.030
AT&amp;T, NOVARTIS and Fastly,

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.760
have all really stepped in to help

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.950
us close some of that gap,

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.980
but we need more so, if you find yourself

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.360
in a position to do so, please
think about supporting us

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.010
and if you have any questions,

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.730
you can start adding them
to the message boards

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:25.423
and we'll try to get
trough as many as we can.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.160
So, Meaghan we have a really
great question from YouTube

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:34.590
from Gamermash, I'm going
through high school next year,

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.240
I'm already worrying
about working too much,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.590
how can I keep up so I'm
ready for high school?

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.450
- That's a great question
and first things first,

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.860
take a deep breath.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:48.090
I'm certain that you have a
great support system around you

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:50.220
and remember that you're not in it alone

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.280
a lot of students are asking themselves

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:53.610
that question right now, right?

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.400
You've had a huge disruption to the end

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.340
of your Middle school experience

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.610
and taking on high school

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.660
is such a huge challenge in and of itself.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.720
I was a high school teacher for nine years

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.590
and I always loved that
fresh look of new students

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.280
and how they are eager to learn

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.870
and still trying to adapt

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.800
and find who they are as they change.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.260
Well we've got some great resources

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.320
to help you on the academic
side of that, for sure.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.540
We have a learning plans for Math

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.750
that we have things to
help you with the content

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.270
you're looking at right now,
in terms of daily schedules,

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.340
to help you stay on track

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.400
with what you're trying
to finish right now

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.980
and then there's learning
plans for over the summer,

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.260
to either look more at
what you might be learning

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.090
to finish eighth grade or
maybe to get you a step ahead,

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.490
so maybe that content
doesn't feel as intimidating

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:39.000
as you step trough that first door.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.210
The other thing we might
be able to support you,

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:44.570
is we have some great
grove mindset content.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.466
And that might be able to help

00:03:45.466 --> 00:03:47.320
you frame what you're learning,

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:50.350
and that experience, and
how you can prepare yourself

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:54.150
for learning across subjects
and even beyond the academic.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.960
And so I would really take a look

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.680
at both our daily schedules,

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.070
and our weekly learning plans

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.300
that you can see on the screen right now,

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.330
to get ahead in what you might be learning

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.233
in Math, come the fall.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.450
- Yeah, I would just
plug the learning plans,

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.400
we just hosted a Parent webinar last week

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.620
on how to best utilize it,
it was really for parents

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.300
but it's also, as a student,
you can use that as well.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.670
It's really just a way
to add a lot of structure

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.210
and to make sure that,
you know the summer slide

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.840
really doesn't get amplified,

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.160
especially in a time of shool closers.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.290
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.580
- We have a question on
YouTube from Jrfoster,

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.610
what are some of your
recommended books for teenagers

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.280
to read during this quarantine?

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:41.520
I can pitch something, so
right now I've been reading,

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.510
Percy Jackson and The Olympians,

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.170
with my nice and nephews,

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.210
we're on book two, Sea of Monsters.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:49.070
It's way better than the movies were,

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:52.010
I find it's really action packed

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:55.130
and we also have a
recommended reading list

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:57.130
from our Khan Academy Staff.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.520
Meaghan do you have a recommendation?

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.870
- First of all, I
absolutely love those books,

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:02.930
I read them a few years ago

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.618
and I'm with you Dan, I say the books

00:05:04.618 --> 00:05:07.910
are significantly better than the movie.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.560
Some books for high school
students well that's,

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.160
I mean there's plenty of things out there.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.700
I'm a Harry Potter fan myself

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:14.950
and I think that you know,

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.880
that's always a great thing to look into.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:18.713
The other thing is,

00:05:18.713 --> 00:05:20.810
I know there's some suggestive
reading list out there,

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:22.440
I mean some of our staff has provided

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.600
some suggested reading lists

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.690
on that same, keep learning, micro site

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.630
that we shared on the screen a moment ago.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.210
And so I would definitely take a look,

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.580
at some of their suggestions

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.630
because we've some really wonderful people

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:35.530
on staff who have put some deep thought

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.760
into what they might suggest.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.520
The other thing I would say is that

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.260
the important thing is
that you're reading.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:45.860
And so, I think it's often
underestimated that while

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.930
it's great that you know,
maybe you're looking

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.340
for some recommended
books from your teachers

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.460
or from you know maybe our staff

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:53.930
but the important thing
is that you're reading.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:55.740
So, if there's something that interest you

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.730
and is really engaging you,

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:01.150
whether that be, you know a blog or a book

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:04.440
or you know maybe it's something else

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.300
I can't even think of right now,

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.880
but as long as you're reading,

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.380
what's really important is
that you're engaging yourself

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.973
and more than specifically
any individual book.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.430
- Meaghan, we have a question
on YouTube from Eliot H,

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.980
it's actually for both of us.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.640
What are our roles at Khan Academy?

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.160
How long have we been here?

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:28.559
And how has Khan Academy
changed during your Tenure?

00:06:28.559 --> 00:06:31.630
So, I'm on the marketing team,
I lead the channel marketers

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:34.370
and our product marketing folks here,

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.882
and I've been at Khan Academy
