from Thasha Wright Knocks.

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.720
My kids have been using
Khan for many years,

00:23:22.720 --> 00:23:24.599
how do I get them to
watch instructional videos

00:23:24.599 --> 00:23:26.390
not done by Sal.

00:23:26.390 --> 00:23:28.330
They only want Sal kinda like

00:23:28.330 --> 00:23:29.860
when Steve left Blue's Clues.

00:23:29.860 --> 00:23:32.556
I did love Steve on Blue's Clues as well,

00:23:32.556 --> 00:23:35.400
so I definitely sympathize here.

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:38.373
I don't have a great answer
for this Meaghan, maybe you do?

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:41.520
- I think that's a tough one,

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:46.310
we all get comfortable with
what we know and change is hard.

00:23:46.310 --> 00:23:49.930
I think even I, hearing other voices,

00:23:49.930 --> 00:23:53.400
other the Sal sometimes, you
know throws me for a loop,

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:57.810
but understanding that there's
so much value in diversity

00:23:57.810 --> 00:24:01.270
and being able to hear other
voices and see other faces.

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:04.060
and so, I think just keep encouraging them

00:24:04.060 --> 00:24:07.380
and maybe if you can find one other voice

00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:08.760
or one other thing that interests them,

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:10.890
maybe if the topic is interesting first

00:24:10.890 --> 00:24:13.270
and then the voice narrating that

00:24:13.270 --> 00:24:15.610
or learning alongside your students,

00:24:15.610 --> 00:24:17.020
you know, help support that.

00:24:17.020 --> 00:24:19.730
but I would definitely say Sal's voice

00:24:19.730 --> 00:24:20.920
is absolutely wonderful.

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:24.310
Obviously, of course we're
huge fans here at Khan Academy,

00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:27.370
but being able to support diverse voices

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:29.410
and views is really important.

00:24:29.410 --> 00:24:31.190
And I would say even on our own site,

00:24:31.190 --> 00:24:34.390
if you look at some of
our grammar content,

00:24:34.390 --> 00:24:36.150
you'll hear our colleague David.

00:24:36.150 --> 00:24:38.950
Or if you look at some
of our history content,

00:24:38.950 --> 00:24:40.700
you'll hear our colleague Kim.

00:24:40.700 --> 00:24:44.440
So, even starting
elsewhere on Khan Academy,

00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:47.340
look around, you'll hear some
other voices other than Sal.

00:24:48.410 --> 00:24:51.580
- Yeah, and I would also say
I mean, the other thing is,

00:24:51.580 --> 00:24:53.500
try to introduce something new everyday

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:55.890
and if your child doesn't like that,

00:24:55.890 --> 00:25:00.890
or doesn't respond, try
a different instructor

00:25:02.590 --> 00:25:06.080
and hopefully they'll pick
up on somebody else as well.

00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:10.262
So, Meaghan we have a
question for you on Facebook

00:25:10.262 --> 00:25:14.900
Sahid, sorry if I'm
